[{:db/id "q-99032/selection/90c9e9181c54cd8186be59b59de2045682d288ad39169152d717ec83771c350a" :answer/id #uuid "b7c58a7c-9d19-5b06-8aa7-58480d5eae11" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-1$ and $x=-7$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99032/selection/f731efd3c86e79bd1ec82599defe86bf97299cbd1a69ebcdb5508161f7a441f2" :answer/id #uuid "05923af4-d390-526c-8df8-e27fd8bb88c8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ and $x=4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99032/selection/23df3cc8fd5bde0e386e55c7795c32c23c3fa77f1d5949a3eb5b26ccfe49a47a" :answer/id #uuid "6e87c79c-fea0-559e-934f-f6ccc2921839" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=3$ and $x=5$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99032/selection/8e4d4a3b045de0431ac85bcd6cc7267a709c597f961b6ccc66ccc78e25a8d60e" :answer/id #uuid "144e1c59-0d9c-5a61-9aeb-aaaf350922e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-3$ and $x=4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99032/selection/96235c743b6ccb17ce05eb1acda8cfc6f06a51f0f11b853a44d9c8d17f39b1e1" :answer/id #uuid "f36736f3-8c5e-5f4d-bf2b-ff007bc07c98" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-2$ and $x=-6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-99032/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ccf8016-a8fc-5c9d-8364-dcdd8611c233" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-99032/selection/90c9e9181c54cd8186be59b59de2045682d288ad39169152d717ec83771c350a" :answer-field/choices ["q-99032/selection/90c9e9181c54cd8186be59b59de2045682d288ad39169152d717ec83771c350a" "q-99032/selection/f731efd3c86e79bd1ec82599defe86bf97299cbd1a69ebcdb5508161f7a441f2" "q-99032/selection/23df3cc8fd5bde0e386e55c7795c32c23c3fa77f1d5949a3eb5b26ccfe49a47a" "q-99032/selection/8e4d4a3b045de0431ac85bcd6cc7267a709c597f961b6ccc66ccc78e25a8d60e" "q-99032/selection/96235c743b6ccb17ce05eb1acda8cfc6f06a51f0f11b853a44d9c8d17f39b1e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-99032" :question/id #uuid "8a08e4af-7f63-5439-b490-91f36e22b19e" :question/math-academy-id "q-99032" :question/problem "Find the critical points of the function $f(x)={x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+21x+23.$" :question/worked-solution "A critical point of $f(x)$ is a point $x=c$ in the domain of $f$ such that either ${f}^{′}(c)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(c)$ does not exist.\n\nDifferentiating $f(x),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}+12{x}^{2}+21x+23) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+24x+21.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to find the critical points:\n\n- First, we compute the points where ${f}^{′}(c)=0.$ We set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+24x+21 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+8x+7 & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(x+7) & =0 \\\\ x & =-1,\\,-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has stationary points at $x=-1$ and $x=-7.$\n\n- Second, we note that ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists for all values of $x$ in the domain of $f(x).$ So $f(x)$ has no non-stationary critical points.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the critical points of $f(x)$ are $x=-1$ and $x=-7.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-99032/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4bd2a8e-357a-5f22-bd50-608e68432a8d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-99032"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-21495"] :question/problem "Find the critical points of the function $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}+24x+9.$" :question/worked-solution "A critical point of $f(x)$ is a point $x=c$ in the domain of $f$ such that either ${f}^{′}(c)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(c)$ does not exist.\n\nDifferentiating $f(x),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-15{x}^{2}+24x+9) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}-30x+24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to find the critical points:\n\n- First, we compute the points where ${f}^{′}(c)=0.$ We set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-30x+24 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-5x+4 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)(x-4) & =0 \\\\ x & =1,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has stationary points at $x=1$ and $x=4.$\n\n- Second, we note that ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists for all values of $x$ in the domain of $f(x).$ So $f(x)$ has no non-stationary critical points.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the critical points of $f(x)$ are $x=1$ and $x=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-131188/selection/ea2041f20c4b14bff500247c5888e7e0eb5fe45d5d45df3195d04364542f52ba" :answer/id #uuid "c9824cdf-3af6-564a-9129-f1a551721ee5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-4$ and $x=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131188/selection/33f0f660888ccc839f810c937f8948a552d5d8465ee889d1dee51395e8f99b3d" :answer/id #uuid "54fbfe87-1aae-5994-a8a6-dcb155d90045" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-6$ and $x=3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131188/selection/9271d00c8d1d7103d1bc87025178cab8596acabb20f5a193f80378edfc306f25" :answer/id #uuid "df14003c-31e1-58e7-9ad1-d01204e7091e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-3$ and $x=6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131188/selection/f31aa950d2003e93a245712eee4481c34af7dd5eb25e80ed0ace0e07e29b8fc8" :answer/id #uuid "285a0db0-558f-57ba-924c-e6d9319d269e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-4$ and $x=6$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131188/selection/8e4d4a3b045de0431ac85bcd6cc7267a709c597f961b6ccc66ccc78e25a8d60e" :answer/id #uuid "8b86c963-27af-515f-a734-1123ac78b729" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-3$ and $x=4$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-131188/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "71c29374-a391-5932-a35e-e000c60c287e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-131188/selection/8e4d4a3b045de0431ac85bcd6cc7267a709c597f961b6ccc66ccc78e25a8d60e" :answer-field/choices ["q-131188/selection/ea2041f20c4b14bff500247c5888e7e0eb5fe45d5d45df3195d04364542f52ba" "q-131188/selection/33f0f660888ccc839f810c937f8948a552d5d8465ee889d1dee51395e8f99b3d" "q-131188/selection/9271d00c8d1d7103d1bc87025178cab8596acabb20f5a193f80378edfc306f25" "q-131188/selection/f31aa950d2003e93a245712eee4481c34af7dd5eb25e80ed0ace0e07e29b8fc8" "q-131188/selection/8e4d4a3b045de0431ac85bcd6cc7267a709c597f961b6ccc66ccc78e25a8d60e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-131188" :question/id #uuid "19a51c3a-961d-51e8-839d-dcbc2e643a8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-131188" :question/problem "Find the critical points of the function $f(x)=2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-72x.$" :question/worked-solution "A critical point of $f(x)$ is a point $x=c$ in the domain of $f$ such that either ${f}^{′}(c)=0$ or ${f}^{′}(c)$ does not exist.\n\nDifferentiating $f(x),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}-72x) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}-6x-72.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to find the critical points:\n\n- First, we compute the points where ${f}^{′}(c)=0.$ We set the derivative equal to zero, and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-6x-72 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-x-12 & =0 \\\\ (x-4)(x+3) & =0 \\\\ x & =-3,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has stationary points at $x=-3$ and $x=4.$\n\n- Second, we note that ${f}^{′}(x)$ exists for all values of $x$ in the domain of $f(x).$ So $f(x)$ has no non-stationary critical points.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the critical points of $f(x)$ are $x=-3$ and $x=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-131188/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f4bd2a8e-357a-5f22-bd50-608e68432a8d"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-131188"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-99019/selection/d1b8c3adb0ced2a3b27706bdf7fd2f4ed1e013b536fdc5ee5d51555269d118ca" :answer/id #uuid "9b042981-4567-54bb-97a1-e